# Expectation record for 14_abi_calling_convention/003_mixed_parameter_classes.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 003_mixed_parameter_classes
area               = 14_abi_calling_convention
description        = Twenty-six interleaved parameters -- five repetitions of (int, double, double, pointer, 8-byte two-int aggregate) followed by an int variant tag, giving sixteen integer-class and ten floating-class consumers -- so that both register files are exhausted and each target's classification rules are exercised together rather than one class at a time, in a folded and a volatile-runtime variant
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour by construction:
- NO ARITHMETIC REACHES THE OUTPUT. Every one of the twenty-six parameters is only printed,
  never combined, so no signed integer overflow is possible on any printed value. The only
  arithmetic in the program is the loop counter's increment, bounded at five. Every integer
  literal is small -- the largest magnitude is 3005, in the array the pointers designate --
  and every one is representable in int on all four targets.
- Every floating value is a dyadic rational with a denominator of at most sixteen, so it is
  exactly representable in binary64, and its exact decimal expansion terminates at or before
  the fourth decimal place, which is the precision the program prints with. The printed text
  is therefore exact: no rounding decision is taken and i686's x87 extended intermediate
  precision cannot perturb a result. No non-finite value, no negative zero and no division
  appears.
- No shift operator appears, so no shift count can be out of range.
- POINTER DISCIPLINE. The five pointers passed are addresses of elements of a static const
  int array of five elements, formed with constant indices strictly inside its bounds: the
  folded call takes them as &ptgt[0] through &ptgt[4], and the runtime call reads those same
  five addresses back out of a volatile array initialised with them. Each is dereferenced in
  the callee and only the pointed-to int is printed. No pointer value is printed, no
  one-past-end pointer is formed, and no pointer is converted to an integer.
- AGGREGATE DISCIPLINE. Only named members are read back. No padding byte is printed,
  compared or memcmp'd, and no aggregate is inspected byte-wise, so the fact that a
  two-int aggregate's layout is the compiler's business cannot reach the output. The
  aggregate has no padding to carry in the first place: measured on all four targets, it is
  8 bytes with 4-byte alignment, exactly two ints' worth, so a by-value copy of it moves no
  indeterminate byte either.
- No read of uninitialized storage: each of the five runtime aggregates has BOTH of its
  members assigned before it is passed, one volatile read per statement.
- No object is modified twice between sequence points.
- NOTHING DEPENDS ON UNSPECIFIED EVALUATION ORDER, and this is enforced structurally
  rather than argued. An access to a volatile object IS an observable side effect and the
  order in which a call's arguments are evaluated is unspecified, so every volatile datum
  is read exactly once, in a statement of its own, and only the resulting plain locals are
  passed. Machine-checked on this branch by flattening main into statements and counting
  references to its volatile objects: there are seventeen volatile accesses in all -- four
  in the loop body, the tag, ten aggregate members and the two function-pointer loads --
  and NO statement holds more than one. The snapshots cost nothing in coverage, because
  each is itself a load from volatile storage that the optimizer may neither fold nor
  elide, so every value the callee receives was genuinely materialised at run time and
  marshalled through the ABI; what changed is only that the loads are now SEQUENCED rather
  than unordered.
- Hermetic, as constraint C4 requires: every input is a literal in the source. Nothing is
  opened, no socket is created, no environment variable and no program argument is read, no
  clock and no random source is consulted, and no storage is obtained from the heap.
- main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires.
- Verified empirically on this branch with gcc 13.4.0, which is why this record sanctions no
  gate deviation and omits ub_audit_flags: the default strict warning gate
  (-Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror) produces zero
  diagnostics, both in the gate's own compile-only form and additionally at -O0, -O1 and
  -O2; and the sanitizer gate (-fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all,
  native and dynamically linked) builds and then runs to completion with empty stderr, exit
  status 0, and stdout byte-identical to the golden record below.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
WHICH REGISTER FILES ARE EXHAUSTED. Twenty-six parameters arranged as five repetitions of
(int, double, double, pointer, 8-byte aggregate) followed by an integer tag: sixteen
integer-class consumers -- five ints, five pointers, five aggregates and the tag, each 8-byte
aggregate taking a single integer slot -- and ten floating-class consumers, so BOTH files are
exhausted on System V AMD64 (six integer registers, eight SSE), AAPCS64 (x0-x7, v0-v7) and
LP64D (a0-a7, fa0-fa7), while System V i386 cdecl marshals all twenty-six on the stack. The
documented rows are docs/technical-specifications.md line 546 (x86-64), line 553 (i686
cdecl), line 559 (AAPCS64) and line 565 (LP64D). The interleaving is the point -- it forces
each ABI to advance its integer and floating allocators independently and in step, which is
exactly where the four conventions disagree.

THE CALL BARRIER. Every call this program makes to the function whose ABI boundary is
under test goes through a FILE-SCOPE volatile FUNCTION POINTER, and that is load-bearing
rather than stylistic. A C11 volatile lvalue must be re-read on every access, so no
conforming compiler may assume which function the pointer designates: it can neither
inline the callee nor clone it, and it must marshal the arguments exactly as the ABI
prescribes because it cannot know what will receive them. This is plain standard C rather
than a compiler attribute, so both sides of oracle (a) honour it for the same reason and
neither needs to support an extension for the barrier to hold. It also makes the
function-pointer load the ONLY volatile access in each call expression, which is what
keeps the one-side-effecting-argument rule satisfied.

WHY THE BARRIER EXISTS, MEASURED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS ON THIS BRANCH WITH GCC 13.4.0. Take it
away, call the function by name, and the documented boundary stops being crossed at the two
optimization levels where it matters most. With the constant call site alone, no
take_mixed26 is emitted at all at -O1 or -O2 on any of the four targets: a static function
reached from one caller is inlined into it whatever its size, and twenty-six parameters are
then classified by nobody. With two call sites whose arguments are all compile-time
constants, -O2 emits only take_mixed26.constprop.0 -- a clone with the constants folded in --
on all four targets, so the boundary that does get crossed is not the documented one. With
the barrier in place the committed program measures clean: take_mixed26 is emitted unmodified
at -O0, -O1 and -O2 on all four targets, with no .constprop and no .isra clone in any of the
twelve objects, and each call site is a genuine indirect call (call *%rax through the loaded
pointer on x86-64, blr x8 on AArch64).

WHAT IS KEPT OFF STDOUT, AND WHY. Width normalisation first: only int and double are passed
as scalars and the aggregate holds two ints, so nothing whose width differs by target can
reach the output. sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) were measured as 4 on i686 and 8 on
x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64 (docs/technical-specifications.md lines 457-462); no long,
size_t, ptrdiff_t, intptr_t or pointer value is printed, and the conversion specifications
used are exactly %d for int, %.4f for double and %s for char * -- %ld, %lu, %zu and %p
appear nowhere. Pointers are passed but never printed: only the pointed-to int is, in
accordance with the corpus rule that pointer facts may appear only as differences,
comparisons and alignment residues. No sizeof and no _Alignof result is printed either,
which is what keeps the aggregate's size, alignment and padding off stdout altogether: they
are the compiler's business, and the program is written to depend on none of them. Plain
char signedness is implementation-defined and was measured as signed on x86_64 and i686 and
unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64; no plain-char value is printed, and char appears only as
const char *. long double has three different representations across the four targets
(measured 16, 12, 16 and 16 bytes; x87 80-bit versus IEEE binary128) and is absent from this
program entirely -- using it would import a difference that has nothing to do with parameter
passing. That type is covered by 13_floating_point/004_long_double_target_restricted, whose
record disables oracle (b) alone, with the measured reason recorded and the
expected-divergence marker XD-TYPE-LONGDOUBLE-001 scoping that oracle.

NOTHING IS NARROWED. No target is dropped, no oracle is disabled and this record carries no
expected-divergence marker: a cross-backend divergence here is a GENUINE FINDING rather than
an implementation-defined difference, because nothing implementation-defined reaches the
output. Measured on this branch with gcc 13.4.0 and the matching i686, aarch64 and riscv64
cross drivers, executed natively and under QEMU user-mode 10.1.0: stdout is byte-identical
and the exit status is 0 in all twelve target-and-optimization-level cells.
END
